From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BipAgents <patches@bipagents.local>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:00:25 +0100
Subject: Calls to a call_context server go side by side per session

Hermes sent one tools/call at a time to each MCP server (`_rpc_lock`): a call waiting minutes for its person (an
approval card) held every other conversation's calls to that server. For a server whose config says
`call_context: true`, calls of one Hermes session still go one at a time, different sessions' side by side (the SDK
tells requests apart by their JSON-RPC id on stdio and HTTP alike). The server's own RPCs (tools/list, keepalive,
refresh, a call without a session) stay exclusive and wait for the calls in flight without holding new ones back;
`locked()` stays true while any call runs (recycling and keepalive see a busy server). An elicitation finds its
call's context by the session its `_meta` names, else the only call in flight, else it is declined. Every other
server: unchanged.

BipAgents patch, documented in hermes/patches/README.md of the BipAgents repository.

Bip-Patch: 0029-mcp-call-context-per-session
